{"title":"Virginia fact of the day","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/925800776/0/marginalrevolution~Virginia-fact-of-the-day.html","date":1759663752000,"content":"<blockquote><p>Virginia saw one of the smallest increases in electricity costs in the nation this past year, per new federal <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.eia.gov/electricity/data/browser/\" target=\"_blank\">data</a>, but it could get even higher as data centers proliferate statewide…</p>\r\n<p><strong>By the numbers: </strong>Between May 2024 and May 2025, the average cost of electricity for residential customers in Virginia rose about 3%, from 14.95 cents to 15.41 cents, according to the U.S. Energy Information Administration.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>The negative media bias aside, I find this encouraging.  OK, “…could get even higher,” but the nationwide average was 6.5%.  Here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.axios.com/local/richmond/2025/08/06/electricity-costs-bills-data-centers-ai-virginia\" target=\"_blank\">the full story</a>.  Via <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/AndyMasley/status/1974702025222095028\" target=\"_blank\">Andy Masley</a>.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/10/virginia-fact-of-the-day-3.html\">Virginia fact of the day</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/925800776/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/925800776/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/925800776/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://as